schema: "0.4"
id: fim-notebook-livebook-and-widgets-kino-maplibre-04-edge-integration-state-accessibility
type: visualization
quality: high
solution: kino-maplibre
category: notebook-livebook-and-widgets
variant: edge-integration-state-accessibility
prompt:
  system: |-
    You are a senior Elixir Livebook geospatial engineer. Output only one complete ASCII Elixir Livebook code cell for Kino.MapLibre. No Markdown fences, no prose outside code. Prioritize validation, fallback behavior, accessibility, and safe map integration.
  text: |-
    Create a Kino.MapLibre edge/integration cell that validates incoming coordinate records, rejects swapped or out-of-range lat/lng values, converts valid rows to GeoJSON, and renders a map plus a validation table. Include a fallback basemap style or a clear no-tile fallback, a text summary for screen-reader users, and optional dynamic update_geojson behavior for corrected records.

    Requirements: document Livebook compatibility, {longitude, latitude} ordering, required row fields, validation errors, and fallback data; never embed API keys; keep inline GeoJSON bounded; include accessibility labels and non-map summaries; include safe execution checks for remote tile failures, untrusted coordinates, oversized feature sets, eval, shell calls, credentials, and browser performance.
  provider_options:
    max_tokens: 8192
    temperature: 0.2
    top_p: 0.9
output:
  text_format: elixir
  artifact_kind: livebook-kino-maplibre-edge-cell
  formats:
  - format: exs
evaluation:
  checklist:
  - "Import check: generated code installs kino_maplibre and kino, validates coordinate records, builds GeoJSON, and renders Kino.MapLibre."
  - "Notebook compatibility: comments identify Livebook/Kino and map tile/style fallback expectations."
  - "Reactive state: update_geojson or other dynamic calls operate only on a Kino.MapLibre widget with validated bounded data."
  - "Data shape: input record fields, validation errors, GeoJSON feature schema, and lng/lat order are documented."
  - "Accessibility and fallback: validation table, text map summary, readable labels, and no-tile or fallback data behavior are present."
  - "Safe execution: no embedded API keys, unbounded feature sets, unsafe remote assumptions, eval, shell commands, credentials, or unvalidated coordinates."
  rubric:
  - name: Format validity
    weight: 30
    criteria:
    - "Output is one complete ASCII Elixir Livebook code cell with no Markdown fences or explanatory wrapper."
    - "The code is valid and separates validation, GeoJSON conversion, and map rendering."
    - "The map sources and layers are built with supported MapLibre DSL structure."
  - name: Semantic completeness
    weight: 30
    criteria:
    - "Implements coordinate validation, error reporting, fallback data, map rendering, and optional dynamic updates."
    - "Uses Kino.MapLibre-specific rules for coordinate order, sources, layers, and widget mutators."
    - "Includes notebook/livebook compatibility, reactive state, data shape, accessibility, fallback, and safe execution checks."
  - name: UX/structural quality
    weight: 25
    criteria:
    - "Users can inspect both valid features and rejected records without relying on map visuals alone."
    - "Map labels, summary text, and validation messages are readable and accessible."
    - "Fallback and tile-error behavior is explicit."
  - name: Robustness
    weight: 15
    criteria:
    - "Handles swapped coordinates, out-of-range values, empty records, missing properties, duplicate ids, and tile failures."
    - "Keeps data deterministic and bounded."
    - "Documents API-key and network boundaries without requiring credentials."
  pass_conditions:
  - "All required YAML fields are present and the generated artifact is one valid ASCII Elixir Livebook cell."
  - "Rubric weights are exactly Format validity 30, Semantic completeness 30, UX/structural quality 25, Robustness 15."
  - "The prompt requires notebook/livebook compatibility, reactive state, data shape, accessibility, fallback, and safe execution checks."
  - "The solution remains Kino.MapLibre-centered and treats geospatial integration data as validated local input."
tags:
- fim
- notebook-livebook-and-widgets
- livebook
- kino-maplibre
- edge-integration-state-accessibility
